{
 "spec": "EXTENSIONS.md Section 12",
 "format": [
  "Each case is the byte sequence of one direction of a packet stream (\"hex\"), a sequence of RFC 9297 capsules: Type (i), Length (i), Value.",
  "A consumer decodes \"hex\" from the start with a receive bound of \"max_payload\" payload bytes, as if the bytes were followed by the end of the stream (FIN).",
  "Type 0x00 is DATAGRAM: its Value is Context ID (i) followed by the payload; each yields one entry of \"packets\" ({context, payload hex}), in order.",
  "A capsule of any other type is skipped; \"skipped\" counts them.",
  "\"error\" is null when the bytes decode cleanly to the end. Otherwise it is \"oversized\" or \"truncated\" and the packets listed are those decoded before the error; a receiver answers either with ZMUX_PACKET_ERROR (RESET_STREAM and STOP_SENDING).",
  "oversized: a Length above max_payload + 8 (any type), detected as soon as the Length is read, or a DATAGRAM whose payload (Value minus Context ID) exceeds max_payload.",
  "truncated: the bytes end inside a capsule (in Type, Length or Value), or a DATAGRAM Value ends inside its Context ID.",
  "\"encode\" true means \"hex\" is also the canonical encoding (minimal varints, no other capsules) of \"packets\": a sender that writes these packets as capsules produces exactly these bytes."
 ],
